    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/230> ;
    ilxtr:alertNote """Data source note: Information on the splanchnic nerve comes from ISBN13:978-1608312948.
Physiological condition: Sympathetic innervation is known to undergo dynamic functional and/or anatomical changes during gestation. This has been observed in several species including rats and humans. Vera et al (1997) https://doi.org/10.1016/s0006-8993(96)01107-9.""" ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote "The term \"celiac\" was deleted from \"aorticorenal ganglion\" because it will bring more confusion than clarity here. In Houdeau (1998) in figure 7 the ganglia are depicted together. From the literature it seems celiac ganglion gives rise and is closely connected with aorticorenal so it is safe to include the aorticorenal ganglion here. 2) The original destination \"upper uterine blood vessel of the myometrium or endometrium\" changed to \"blood vessel of the upper uterus\" that covers the vasculature of the upper uterine segment. Houdeau (1998) using retrograde tracing shows that the epicenter of the origin of the postganglionic fibers in the paravertebral sympathetic chain is at T12-L1, but the spread ranges from T10 to L2. Information on the splanchnic nerve comes from ISBN13:978-1608312948." ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "female L1 sympathetic chain ganglion T12 sympathetic chain ganglion T13 sympathetic chain ganglion (with-axons-in aorticorenal ganglion least splanchnic nerve lesser splanchnic nerve lumbar splanchnic nerve ovarian nerve plexus) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in blood vessel of the upper uterus) (implies Rattus norvegicus Sympathetic Post-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
