    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/251> ;
    ilxtr:alertNote """Connectivity ambiguity: In the absence of experimental data on the specific spinal cord level from which this connection arises we decided to include all sympathetic spinal cord levels from T1 to L2. 
Spatial extent: Houdeau (1998) using retrograde tracing shows that the epicenter of the origin of the postganglionic fibers in the paravertebral sympathetic chain is at T12-L1, but the spread ranges from T10 to L2.
Data source note: Information on the splanchnic nerve comes from ISBN13:978-1608312948.
Physiological condition: Sympathetic innervation is known to undergo dynamic functional and/or anatomical changes during gestation. This has been observed in several species including rats and humans. Vera et al (1997) https://doi.org/10.1016/s0006-8993(96)01107-9.""" ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote "Wulf (2023) https://doi.org/10.3389/fncel.2023.999253 mentioned about the sympathetic innervation “The SPNs reside in the intermediolateral cell column (IML) of thoracolumbar spinal cord segments T1-L2 (McLachlan and Oldfield, 1981; Oldfield and McLachlan, 1981; Anderson et al., 1989)”. In light of the absense of experimental data on the level of the spinal cord that this connection arises from and suggested by the knowledge expert we decided to include all the sympathetic spinal cord from T1-L2. Information on the splanchnic nerve comes from ISBN13:978-1608312948." ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "female lumbar subsegment of spinal cord thoracic subsegment of spinal cord (with-axons-in lumbar splanchnic nerve thoracic splanchnic nerve) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in suprarenal ganglion) (projecting-onto neuron type femrep 35) (implies Rattus norvegicus Sympathetic Pre-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
    ilxtr:literatureCitation <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jasi.2014.04.008>,
        <https://uilx.org/tgbugs/u/r/isbn-13/978-1608312948> ;
