    ilxtr:alertNote """Spatial extent: In Gerandai (1998) https://doi.org/10.1159/000054372 they observed a spread of labeled cells in the IML from T4-L3 but the epicenter was T9-T10.
Physiological condition: Sympathetic innervation is known to undergo dynamic functional and/or anatomical changes during gestation. This has been observed in several species including rats and humans. Vera et al (1997) https://doi.org/10.1016/s0006-8993(96)01107-9.""" ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote "Originally the population had as via \"splanchnic nerve\" but considering it is a communication between spinal cord and sympathetic chain \"white rami communicantes\" is representing the route more appropriately. \"In Gerandai (1998) 10.1159/000054372 they observed labeled cells in the IML from T4-L3 but the epicenter was T9-T10." ;
