    ilxtr:alertNote """Laterality difference: The references indicate a laterality difference in the innervation of the ovary. 
Physiological condition: Sympathetic innervation is known to undergo dynamic functional and/or anatomical changes during gestation. This has been observed in several species including rats and humans. Vera et al (1997) https://doi.org/10.1016/s0006-8993(96)01107-9.
Alert 3: Pastelin 2017 and 2023 - SON innervation includes both ipsilateral and contralateral postganglionic fibers—i.e., some fibers cross to innervate the ovary from the opposite side's ganglia (Contralateral CG and SG also labeled when injecting True Blue (TB) tracer into the right ovary). OPN innervation appears mostly ipsilateral, with no contralateral fibers reported.""" ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "female suprarenal ganglion (with-axon-in SON) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in left ovary right ovary) (implies Rattus norvegicus Sympathetic Post-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
