            owl:onProperty ilxtr:hasInstanceInTaxon ;
            owl:someValuesFrom NCBITaxon:9606 ] ;
    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/163> ;
    ilxtr:alertNote """Spatial extent: The spinal levels T10-L1 are mentioned in the references below as the sympathetic innervation of the female reproductive system arises from the superior hypogastric plexus, which in turn arises mainly from the spinal levels mentioned above. Janig et al (1987), table 2, shows these spinal levels as origins of the preganglionic fibers innervating the female reproductive organs. This is supported also by Gray’s Anatomy (40th edition) which states that sympathetic fibers to the uterus are derived from neurons in the last thoracic and first lumbar segments. However, often the splanchnic nerves to the abdomen and pelvis are grouped into “abdominopelvic splanchnic nerves” (see Clinically Oriented Anatomy, Lippincott Williams and Wilkins, 5th ed). It’s possible that the preganglionic neurons spread between T5-L4 with an epicenter at T10-L1.
Physiological condition: Sympathetic innervation is known to undergo dynamic functional and/or anatomical changes during gestation. This has been observed in several species including rats and humans. Vera et al (1997) https://doi.org/10.1016/s0006-8993(96)01107-9.""" ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "female L1 segment of lumbar spinal cord T10 segment of thoracic spinal cord T11 segment of thoracic spinal cord T12 segment of thoracic spinal cord (with-axons-in hypogastric nerve inferior hypogastric nerve plexus superior hypogastric nerve plexus) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in pelvic ganglion) (projecting-onto neuron type femrep 67 neuron type femrep 68 neuron type femrep 69 neuron type femrep 70 neuron type femrep 71 neuron type femrep 72 neuron type femrep 82 neuron type femrep 83) (implies Homo sapiens Sympathetic Pre-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
    ilxtr:literatureCitation <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mpaic.2019.04.003>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/physrev.1987.67.4.1332>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fphar.2014.00017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5005/jp/books/13032_63> ;
