    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/123> ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote """The destinations to both the distal stomach smooth muscle outer longitudinal layer and the distal stomach smooth muscle circular layer include the PDGFR-alpha receptor that is not demonstrated in the modelling of this population.

This population includes non-neuronal cell types (Parietal cell, enteroendocrine cell, ) as targets in the ApiNATOMY model. IN KM Lab meeting 10/23/25, we decide to revisit this scenario to determine if this should be modeled as a forward connection, or a specialized type of forward connection (e.g., synpasesWith) or similar. Otherwise, I updated the modeling in this population matches anatomies and layers as depicted in the model [https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-physiology/apinatomy-models/refs/heads/master/models/sawg-stomach/docs/sawg-stomach.svg]. Also note that this neuron population is identified as inhibitory.

10/30/2025 [ST]: This ApiNATOMY population had a dendrite colocated with the soma, creating a loop. This has been removed.""" ;
