    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/124> ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote """10/30/2025 [ST]: This ApiNATOMY population had a dendrite colocated with the soma, creating a loop. This has been removed.
10/23/2025 [ST]: This population includes non-neuronal cell types (Parietal cell, enteroendocrine cell, chief cell) as targets in the ApiNATOMY model. IN KM Lab meeting 10/23/25, we decided to revisit this scenario to determine if this should be modeled as a forward connection, or a specialized type of forward connection (e.g., synpasesWith) or similar. Otherwise, I updated the modeling in this population matches anatomies and layers as depicted in the model [https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-physiology/apinatomy-models/refs/heads/master/models/sawg-stomach/docs/sawg-stomach.svg]. Also note that this neuron population is identified as excitatory.""" ;
