    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/306> ;
    ilxtr:alertNote """Cross-species inference: The information mentioned in several of the sources on the origin of preganglionic spinal sympathetic fibers seem to be coming from Magni et al., (1983) https://doi.org/10.1016/0165-1838(83)90108-X were they showed that afferent fibers in rats come from T7-T12. The spinal levels are the same in humans. Considering the pre-ganglionic and post-ganglionic fibers meet in the celiac ganglia it has been shown that the spinal fibers that reach there are T5-T12 with an epicenter mostly T7-T12 [Strack (1988) http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0006-8993(88)90132-1].
Laterality difference: There is laterality in the routing of postganglionic populations.""" ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "Intermediolateral nucleus of eighth thoracic segment Intermediolateral nucleus of eleventh thoracic segment Intermediolateral nucleus of ninth thoracic segment Intermediolateral nucleus of seventh thoracic segment Intermediolateral nucleus of tenth thoracic segment Intermediolateral nucleus of twelfth thoracic segment (with-axon-in thoracic splanchnic nerve) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in CSMG) (projecting-onto neuron type liver 106 neuron type liver 108) (implies Rattus norvegicus Sympathetic Pre-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
