    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/157> ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote """Don't say what nerve. Retrograde tracing study in adult guinea pig. "This work directly confirms what is readily deducable from physiological and structural studies; that nerve cell bodies in the small intestine project to the coeliac ganglia (see Introduction). It shows that these cells are confined to the myenteric plexus, as Schofield [23] concluded, and that their numbers increase anally along the small intestine"
Gary: Intestinofugal neurons coming enteric gangla to pre-vertebral ganglia; changed to mesenteric nerve""" ;
    ilxtr:expertConsultant <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8876-8468> ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "Myenteric ganglion of small intestine (with-axon-in Mesenteric nerve) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in celiac ganglion) (implies Cavia porcellus Enteric projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
