    ilxcr:hasComposerURI <https://composer.scicrunch.io/statement/134> ;
    ilxtr:curatorNote "Caroline and Gary; changed to pelvic ganglion from major pelvic ganglion as there are also contributions from the accessory pelvic ganglia based on Keast (1999): In rats the accessory ganglia contribute mainly to the supply of the reproductive organs. (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0074769608617787?via%3Dihub). Also added levels based on Keast and references therein. Ask Janet whether the accessory ganglia contribute to this or whether it should just be major pelvic ganglia. Answer: Yes, the connections are shared among the MPG and AG, so we should change to pelvic ganglion (but map to ILX term until UBERON is changed)." ;
    ilxtr:expertConsultant <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8876-8468>,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2871-3825> ;
    ilxtr:genLabel "L6 parasympathetic nucleus S1 sacral parasympathetic nucleus (with-axon-in pelvic splanchnic nerve) (with-axon-presynaptic-element-in MPG accessory pelvic ganglion) (projecting-onto neuron type mmset4 3a neuron type mmset4 3b neuron type mmset4 3c) (implies Rattus norvegicus Parasympathetic Pre-Ganglionic projection) neuron (sprcnlp)" ;
    ilxtr:literatureCitation <https://doi.org/10.1007/bf00224723>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0074-7696(08)61778-7> ;
