    ilxtr:curatorNote "Needs verification; Ask Janet. Is Fig 1, https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/ar.1092240112, equivalent to the connection in Fig 1 https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0074769606480037#fig0001 but according to Arellano et al: \"The precise axonal composition and role of the cavernous nerve in autonomic innervation of the penis requires further studies since we did not found an anatomical connection of this nerve with the penis.\" Also from Arellano: the cavernous nerve (also known as penile nerve, or main penile nerve) so synonymous" ;
